  "slug": "ev-2026-08-30-legacy-rescore-outcome",
  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T12:05:51.745Z",
  "what": "Outcome of re-scoring the 134 legacy-scored shortlist postings identified in ev-2026-08-30-board-scorer-provenance, on claude-sonnet-5 (the retained reason-tier default).",
  "headline": {
    "shortlist_before": 162,
    "shortlist_after": 63,
    "dropped": 99,
    "legacy_postings_rescored": 134,
    "distinct_scores_legacy_before": 12,
    "distinct_scores_after_rescore": 20,
    "pct_multiple_of_5_before": 92.5,
    "pct_multiple_of_5_after": 79.9,
    "cost_calls": 16
  },
  "interpretation": "Re-scoring on sonnet-5 fixed the specific defect: distinct values across the 134 nearly doubled (12 to 20) and round-number clustering fell (92.5% to 79.9% multiples of five). 99 of 162 shortlisted postings dropped below the 40 floor once actually read, most of them the round-40/45/50 legacy scores that were carrying no real judgment. This is not a full resolution: sonnet-5 itself still returns a multiple of five four times in five, which is a milder version of the same rounding tendency and worth watching rather than treating as solved. The rescore does not change the model-quality question the reference benchmark raised - sonnet-5 correlates only moderately with the Opus reference - it only removes the much larger, purely mechanical defect of a stale scorer with 12 possible outputs.",
